Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 05:45:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Prompt Kit script variants and a production-doc
 spokesperson script
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The video_script flow now resolves a BASE prompt case plus an optional style
VARIANT (marketing / training / social_short), and the spokesperson endpoint
returns a full production doc instead of a bare paragraph.

Prompt Kit
- prompt_case_types.variant_key, with two partial unique indexes so exactly one
  ACTIVE case exists per (flow, variant). Two rather than one because Postgres
  treats each NULL as distinct, which would otherwise allow many base cases.
- loadActiveCasePrompt(flowKey, variantKey) resolves the exact variant, falls
  back to the base case, then to null. An unseeded variant degrades to the
  shared rules rather than failing a paid generation.
- Base blocks compile ahead of the variant's (order + 1000), so a variant only
  states what differs.
- Bundle import/export are variant-aware; the clash check now keys on the
  (flow, variant) pair, which previously would have stripped the flow binding
  off every variant after the first.

Script prompts
- The one-line video_script seed is replaced by nine blocks: speakable-only
  rules, word budget, presenter constraints, truthfulness, voice, the delivery
  cue vocabulary, and a self-check. Three variant cases layer on top.
- New video_script_intake flow: a ~200-token pre-pass that extracts only the
  facts a topic actually asserts and reports the remaining gaps.

cleanScript no longer loses information
- It strips every [bracket] from spoken text, which is right — a voice engine
  must not read a cue — but it did so silently, so [VERIFY] flags vanished.
  cleanScriptDetailed now reports what it removed and collectOpenItems lifts
  the flags into meta.openItems. Beat text keeps its cues via cleanCuedText.
- The flat 2000-character cap is now derived from the request's word budget;
  it silently rejected anything past roughly 45 seconds.

Script inputs
- resolveScriptInputs builds the compiler's Context layer from the brand kit
  (audience, tone, CTA style, brand terms, restricted terms) and the reference
  style profile (structural guidance, measured words-per-minute). Brand values
  resolve server-side from ids; bannedTerms is a union so a client can add
  restrictions but never shorten them. Every value passes through sanitizeLine,
  which flattens newlines so a value cannot forge a prompt section heading.

Studio
- A "what kind of video" step precedes the topic, and a clarify step appears
  only when the intake pass found gaps. Extracted facts are removable chips —
  a wrong extraction must not become an asserted claim.
- Review shows word count, open items, per-beat direction, and pronunciations.
- FLOW_KEYS in the admin UI was missing video_motion, which the server already
  seeded; both new keys are added and the drift is noted in agent memory.

Verified: pnpm typecheck, spec-lint and codegen-drift all clean; 2230 api-server
tests and 87 socialforge test files pass. The five remaining api-server failures
are identical before and after this change (they need real SESSION_SECRET and
Meta credentials).

